Issues.Body:
Copy button doesn't copy what's on screen. On blocks with line numbers it copies the numbers as if they were code, and it eats blank lines.

1. Line numbers, first block on https://angular.dev/best-practices/zone-pollution

Before:
```
1
import { Component, NgZone, OnInit, inject } from '@angular/core';
2
3
@Component(...)
```

After:
```
import { Component, NgZone, OnInit, inject } from '@angular/core';

@Component(...)
```

2. Blank lines, first block on https://angular.dev/guide/signals

Before:
```
const count = signal(0);
// Signals are getter functions - calling them reads their value.
console.log('The count is: ' + count());
```

After:
```
const count = signal(0);

// Signals are getter functions - calling them reads their value.
console.log('The count is: ' + count());
```

Fix grabs the visible `.line` elements and joins their text, so numbers stay out and you get the block as rendered. Tested with real clicks and clipboard reads on 63 blocks across 4 pages.

### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?

forms

### Is this a regression?

No

### Description

I apologize for how specific it is, but it's the most minimal reproduction I was able to do. I believe everything I did should be supported, so the NG01904 exception is unexpected. 

It's best explained by looking at the code:

```ts
interface Row {
  score: number;
}

export interface Model {
  rows: { points: number }[];
}

@Component({
  selector: 'app-orphan-repro-control',
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
  imports: [JsonPipe],
  template: `
    @for (rowField of form; track rowField().value().score) {
      {{ rowField().value() | json }}
    }
  `,
})
export class OrphanReproControlComponent implements FormValueControl<Model> {
  readonly value = model.required<Model>();

  private readonly _viewRows = transformedValue(this.value, {
    parse: (rows: Row[]): { value: Model } => ({
      value: { rows: rows.map((row) => ({ points: row.score })) },
    }),
    format: (dto): Row[] => (dto.rows ?? []).map((row) => ({ score: row.points })),
  });

  readonly form = form(this._viewRows);
}

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  imports: [FormField, OrphanReproControlComponent],
  template: `
    <button (click)="planForm().reset()" type="button">Reset</button>
    <app-orphan-repro-control [formField]="planForm" />
  `,
})
export class App {
  readonly model = signal({ rows: [{ points: 10 }, { points: 20 }] });
  readonly planForm = form(this.model);
}
```

Resetting the parent's form causes the exception bellow. 

If you think this is expected behavior, please explain why this happens and what am I expected to do as a consumer. 

